BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (One simplified control cycle looks like this:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 261.00 Td (HAL / backend drivers collect sensor data) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 250.00 Td (  -> sensor frontends publish stable sensor state) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 239.00 Td (  -> AHRS / EKF estimate vehicle state) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 228.00 Td (  -> vehicle mode chooses desired behavior) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 217.00 Td (  -> navigation and control libraries calculate demands) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 206.00 Td (  -> motors / SRV_Channel convert demands to actuator outputs) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 195.00 Td (  -> HAL / protocol backends write physical outputs) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf 66.00 184.00 Td (  -> logger and GCS report state) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (The important architectural idea is separation of responsibilities:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 141.00 Td (- vehicle code decides behavior) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 127.00 Td (- libraries provide reusable sensing, estimation, navigation, and control) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (- frontends hide backend implementation details) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 99.00 Td (- HAL hides board implementation details) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 85.00 Td (- output layers hide actuator routing and protocol details) Tj ET
